[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m one-shot wrapper (it allocates a VLA, `memcpy`s the caller's data into it, then
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m calls the `static` `inner`, which calls `fma_array` with **all four pointers
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m aliased to the same buffer** and then `printf`s each element). Both are tested
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m directly through their `.so` exports.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 1 — runtime options / modes / flags
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **None.** `grep -nE "if *\(|switch|#if" c_src/src/driver.c` matches nothing in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the function bodies. There is no global state, no init call, no option struct,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no mode/flag parameter and no compile-time `#ifdef` that changes behaviour.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The only conditional in the entire translation unit is the loop guard `i < len`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (lines 30 and 37). So this axis contributes exactly one value and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cross-product below is driven by the remaining axes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 2 — entry point
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `fma_array` (low-level, caller-supplied output buffer, 4 independent pointers)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `driver` (wrapper: internal buffer, full self-aliasing, stdout side effect)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 3 — `len` (input shape / count)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `0`, `1`, `2`, `3` (odd tail), `8`, `17` (odd, non-power-of-two), `64`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (vectorizable), `1000` (multi-block), and negative (`-1`, `INT_MIN`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `len` is the only size/count/width knob: element type is fixed `int`, there is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no stride, no byte order and no format selector.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 4 — pointer aliasing (only meaningful for `fma_array`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The C signature marks `mul1`/`mul2`/`add` as `const int *` but `inner` passes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the *same* buffer as all four arguments, so aliasing is a first-class input
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m shape that the code genuinely distinguishes (each element is read and then
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m written within the same iteration): all-distinct, `out == mul1`, `out == mul2`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `out == add`, `mul1 == mul2` (square), and full self-alias
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `out == mul1 == mul2 == add`. `driver` always exercises the full self-alias.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 5 — value distribution (boundary values)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `small` — |v| ≤ 1000, so `m1*m2 + a` never overflows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `full` — uniform over the whole `i32` range, so overflow happens constantly
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `boundary` — drawn from `{INT_MIN, INT_MIN+1, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, INT_MAX-1, INT_MAX}`
